From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: no content recommendations

"Get content recommendations" (suggested apps and websites in the launcher
and its suggestion chips) is fed by Google's servers. It is off by default
on NickelOS, and its switch is gone from Settings (Search and suggestions,
and the Privacy controls page).

Google's AI features in the same card (Help me read, Help me write, Lobster)
showed only because Chromium's field-trial testing config switched their
experiments on; NickelOS builds without that config (nickel-chrome.bashrc),
so they are off as their code says, and the card does not show them.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ash/preferences/preferences.cc b/chrome/browser/ash/preferences/preferences.cc
index 702d0585312ed..fa07895cba1af 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ash/preferences/preferences.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ash/preferences/preferences.cc
@@ -563,8 +563,10 @@ void Preferences::RegisterProfilePrefs(
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kLoginDisplayPasswordButtonEnabled,
                                 true);
 
+  // NickelOS: suggested content (apps and websites recommended in the
+  // launcher) comes from Google's servers: off, and Settings has no switch.
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
-      prefs::kSuggestedContentEnabled, true,
+      prefs::kSuggestedContentEnabled, false,
       user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_OS_PREF);
 
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kMagicBoostEnabled, true);
diff --git a/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_privacy_page/privacy_hub_subpage.html b/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_privacy_page/privacy_hub_subpage.html
index 57ab0d0a56075..1b8aa1418c396 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_privacy_page/privacy_hub_subpage.html
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_privacy_page/privacy_hub_subpage.html
@@ -113,10 +113,4 @@
   </template>
 </if>
 
-<div class="hr"></div>
-<settings-toggle-button id="contentRecommendationsToggle"
-    pref="{{prefs.settings.suggested_content_enabled}}"
-    label="$i18n{enableSuggestedContent}"
-    sub-label="$i18n{enableSuggestedContentDesc}"
-    learn-more-url="$i18n{suggestedContentLearnMoreURL}">
-</settings-toggle-button>
+<!-- NickelOS: no content recommendations (Google's), so no switch for them. -->
diff --git a/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_search_page/search_and_assistant_settings_card.html b/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_search_page/search_and_assistant_settings_card.html
index 846fd1dda1f24..49fbb0cd0e232 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_search_page/search_and_assistant_settings_card.html
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/ash/settings/os_search_page/search_and_assistant_settings_card.html
@@ -31,14 +31,8 @@
     </cr-link-row>
   </template>
 
-  <settings-toggle-button id="contentRecommendationsToggle"
-      class="hr"
-      icon="os-settings:content-recommend"
-      pref="{{prefs.settings.suggested_content_enabled}}"
-      label="$i18n{enableSuggestedContent}"
-      sub-label="$i18n{enableSuggestedContentDesc}"
-      learn-more-url="$i18n{suggestedContentLearnMoreURL}">
-  </settings-toggle-button>
+  <!-- NickelOS: no content recommendations (Google's), so no switch for
+       them. -->
 
   <!--TODO(b:337868408) learn more link for magicboost-->
   <template is="dom-if" if="[[isMagicBoostFeatureEnabled_]]">
